## Writing Voice — Blood and Purpose

When writing any game text, match this voice:

- **Dark, deliberate, precise.** Every sentence earns its place.
- **Matter-of-fact about violence.** Not gratuitous — honest.
- **Specificity over adjectives.** "The rot seeps through armour" beats "a terrible magical decay."
- **Mechanics stated clearly** after the flavour, never buried in prose.
- **No whimsy.** No "mystical energies." No "ancient power awakens."
- **Avoid D&D clichés.** Rename anything that sounds like a Wizards of the Coast product.
- **The world doesn't care.** It existed before the players and will outlast them.

